From 18343eb537dff1ecaa799d0536342d27a4c98ed7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: Scale the decoded picture down through the
 secondary output

At 3840x2160 and 60 fps the display's plane reads 750 MB/s of NV12. The
video engine's secondary output can write a second picture scaled by 2
or 4 each way while the engine still reconstructs and references the
full one.

A client asks as a stateful decoder's does: S_SELECTION with the COMPOSE
target on CAPTURE, before CAPTURE buffers exist. The ratio is the
smallest of 1, 2 and 4 whose picture fits the rectangle; G_FMT reports
the scaled size. The scaled NV12 picture sits at the start of the buffer
and the full-size reconstruction after it, as P010 already does. 8-bit
H.264 and H.265 only: SDROT_CTRL at 0x240 with addresses at 0x244 and
0x248 for H.264, the H.265 engine's SDRT_CTRL for H.265.

The decoder node kept G_SELECTION and S_SELECTION disabled, its
selection being the encoder's crop; the decoder now answers COMPOSE.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
